9
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:06,000
Anna Harding, played by Emma Corrin.

10
01:03:20,000 --> 01:03:26,000
Nosferatu is a 2024 American Gothic horror film
written and directed by Robert Eggers.

11
01:09:40,000 --> 01:09:46,000
It is a remake of Nosferatu: A Symphony of Horror (1922), which was in
turn inspired by Bram Stoker's novel Dracula (1897).

12
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
It stars Bill Skarsgård, Nicholas Hoult, Lily-Rose Depp, Aaron
Taylor-Johnson, Emma Corrin, and Willem Dafoe.

13
01:22:20,000 --> 01:22:26,000
Development began in 2015, when Eggers planned to make it his second film; he described
it as a passion project, but eventually opted to delay its production.

14
01:28:40,000 --> 01:28:46,000
Skarsgård and Depp were cast in lead roles in September 2022.

15
01:35:00,000 --> 01:35:06,000
Filming took place primarily at Barrandov Studios in
Prague between February and May 2023.

16
01:41:20,000 --> 01:41:26,000
Nosferatu had its world premiere in Berlin on December 2, 2024, and was
theatrically released in the United States by Focus Features on December 25.

17
01:47:40,000 --> 01:47:46,000
The film received positive reviews from critics and was a commercial success, grossing $181.8
million worldwide on a $50 million budget, becoming Eggers' highest-grossing film.

18
01:54:00,000 --> 01:54:06,000
At the 97th Academy Awards, the film earned nominations for Best Cinematography, Best
Costume Design, Best Production Design, and Best Makeup and Hairstyling.

19
02:00:20,000 --> 02:00:26,000
The film explores themes of cold, based on novel or
book, vampire, necrophilia, eroticism.

20
02:06:40,000 --> 02:06:46,000
The tone is dark and thought_provoking.
